<title>USA: Peregrine Real Estate Q3 loss.</title>
<headline>Peregrine Real Estate Q3 loss.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>					     Quarter-Ended September 30</p>
<p>						     1996	    1995</p>
<p>Operating Results:</p>
<p> Total Revenues			    $   6,265    $   6,738</p>
<p> Total Expenses				  7,163	  8,269</p>
<p> Loss from Operations			 ( 898)	(1,531)</p>
<p> Net loss					(1,200)	(1,296)</p>
<p>Net loss attributable to shares</p>
<p> of beneficial interest(a)		 (1,932)	(1,944)</p>
<p> Total Assets				  110,673	135,859</p>
<p>Shareholders' equity (deficit)</p>
<p>accounts attributable to shares</p>
<p>  of beneficial interest		  (14,232)	  6,197</p>
<p>Per Share Results:</p>
<p>Net loss per share</p>
<p>attributable to shares</p>
<p>  of beneficial interest(a)		 (0.40)	 (1.73)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of shares</p>
<p>  of beneficial interest outstanding     4,881	  4,884</p>
<p>Note (a): Includes the effects of stock dividends, discounts and ccretion of discounts on preferred stock.</p>
<p>Peregrine also announced that its previously reported agreement to sell its 76% stock interest in CalREIT to MDC REIT Holdings LLC, an affiliate of the investment banking firm McCown DeLeeuw &amp; Co., had not been approved by the Board of Trustees of CalREIT.  Closing of the transaction is subject to such approval and various other conditions.  Peregrine is currently reviewing its alternatives with respect to the transaction.</p>
